Hi Dan,

On Wed, Nov 6, 2019 at 6:34 PM Daniel Lee <lee...@umich.edu> wrote:
> Hi Phil-
>
> I appreciate you for developing this resourceful package in R! It is a game-changer!
>
> I had a question about DIF. I used the following syntax to conduct DIF for a 18-item measure on a Likert scale (I set the last 3 items as anchor items and freed the factor mean/variance for the comparison group):
>
> MGmodel <- multipleGroup(dat.dif[,c(1:15)], model=1, itemtype = "graded", group, SE=T,
>                          invariance=c('Dis16', 'Dis17', 'Dis18', 'free_means', 'free_variance'))

Note that 'free_variance' should be 'free_var'. Though I like the idea the multiple input names should do the same thing, so I've added a few new aliases on the dev version.

>
> dif1 <- DIF(MGmodel, c('a', "d1", "d2", "d3", "d4"), scheme = 'add_sequential',  p.adjust = 'BH', seq_stat = .01)

'a' is not a parameter in any IRT model in mirt. You probably meant 'a1'.

>
> I then tried to get an output for dif1 (adjuted p-values to report in manuscript), and I got the following output:
> > dif1$adj_pvals
> numeric(0)
>
> I am not sure what I did wrong here, and I would appreciate any and all feedback you have.
> If I did this correctly, and the output indicates no DIF, can I still obtain the p-values somehow?

I can't tell what went wrong in your example without some reproducible data + code. However, the following example worked fine on my end, so perhaps it will be helpful chasing down your bug.

library(mirt)

#single factor
set.seed(12345)
a <- a2 <- matrix(abs(rnorm(15,1,.3)), ncol=1)
d <- d2 <- matrix(rnorm(15,0,.7),ncol=1)
a2[14:15] <- a[14:15] + .5
d2[14:15] <- d[14:15] + c(-.5, .5)
itemtype <- rep('2PL', nrow(a))
N <- 1000
dataset1 <- simdata(a, d, N, itemtype)
dataset2 <- simdata(a2, d2, N, itemtype, mu = .1, sigma = matrix(1.5))
dat <- rbind(dataset1, dataset2)
group <- c(rep('D1', N), rep('D2', N))
models <- 'F1 = 1-15'

mirtCluster()

# first five items as anchors
mod_ref <- multipleGroup(dat, models, group = group,
                         invariance=c(colnames(dat)[1:5], 'free_var','free_means'))
out1 <- DIF(mod_ref, c('a1', 'd'), scheme='add', items2test = 6:15, p.adjust = 'BH')
out1$adj_pvals

out2 <- DIF(mod_ref, c('a1', 'd'), scheme='add_sequential', items2test = 6:15, p.adjust = 'BH')
out2$adj_pvals

HTH.

Phil

