This was just a minimal example, you can change the width of the intervals just by changing the intercept differences. So

diffs <- t(apply(matrix(runif(20*4, 1, 1), 20), 1, cumsum))

would be much wider and allow for more likelihood in each category based on the expected probability functions. If it's helpful try playing around with the itemplot(shiny=TRUE) interface with the 'graded' model. HTH.

Phil

